diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index b677f4e..0f12e7d 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -5,5 +5,21 @@ A small expense ledger. Entries live in a JSON file (`--data` or `$LEDGER_DATA`)
     python -m ledger add 2026-01-05 12.50 food "lunch"
     python -m ledger list
     python -m ledger report --by month
+    python -m ledger export --format csv
+    python -m ledger export --format json --output entries.json
+
+Export requires `--format csv|json` and writes all entries in ascending date order,
+preserving stored order for entries on the same date. Amounts are two-decimal
+strings matching `list`, including negative refunds. CSV has the header
+`date,amount,category,note` and quotes fields as needed. JSON has the shape
+`{"version": 1, "entries": [{"date": "2026-01-05", "amount": "12.50", "category": "food", "note": "lunch"}]}`.
+An empty ledger produces just the CSV header or `{"version": 1, "entries": []}`.
+
+Output goes to standard output by default. `--output FILE` writes a UTF-8 file
+silently; an existing file is preserved unless `--force` is supplied. Export uses
+the same `--data` option (before the command) or `$LEDGER_DATA` as other commands.
+Successful exports exit with status 0. Missing or unsupported formats, existing
+destinations without `--force`, and unwritable destinations exit with status 2,
+one error line on standard error, and no standard output.
 
 Tests: `python -m unittest discover -s tests`.
